{
  "raw": {
    "https://external-careers.jobs.unsw.edu.au/en/job/542439/work-integrated-learning-wil-team-lead": {
      "title": "Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Team Lead",
      "description": "Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Team Lead Apply now Job no: 542439 Work type: Full Time Location: Sydney, NSW Categories: Knowledge Exchange, Management, Healthcare UNSW Faculty of Medicine & Health Employment Type: Full time (35 hours per week) Duration: continuing position Remuneration: Level 7 from $118k plus 17% superannuation contributions and annual leave loading Location: UNSW Kensington Campus, Sydney Must hold full valid working rights to be eligible About UNSW UNSW isn’t like other places you’ve worked. Yes, we’re a large organisation with a diverse and talented community; a community doing extraordinary things. Together, we are driven to be thoughtful, practical, and purposeful in all we do. Taking this combined approach is what makes our work matter. It’s the reason we’re one of the top 20 universities in the world (QS top 20) and a member of Australia’s prestigious Group of Eight. If you want a career where you can thrive, be challenged and do meaningful work, you’re in the right place. About the role The WIL Team Lead is responsible for leading a specialist WIL team and overseeing the delivery of Work Integrated Learning (WIL) services across relevant Medicine & Health programs. This role provides leadership in WIL operations, stakeholder engagement, compliance and continuous improvement to support high-quality student outcomes and effective service delivery. This is an exciting leadership opportunity for a skilled Work Integrated Learning professional to drive the successful delivery of student placement experiences across a complex and dynamic environment. Working closely with academic leaders, health services and external partners, you will lead a specialist team, strengthen operational excellence, support compliance and governance requirements, and identify opportunities for continuous improvement. The role offers the chance to shape WIL processes, implement innovative systems and contribute to high-quality student outcomes while building strong partnerships across the health and education sectors. If you are a collaborative leader with strong stakeholder engagement, project management and operational expertise, this role provides an excellent opportunity to make a meaningful impact. The role reports to the Academic Programs & WIL Manager and will have direct reports. Some Key Skills Required Relevant tertiary qualification with experience or equivalent competence gained through a combination of education, training, and experience. Demonstrated experience in successfully leading and managing a team with proven ability to motivate and create a positive workplace culture to achieve quality outcomes. Demonstrated experience in managing work-integrated learning processes. Demonstrated experience interpreting, applying and advising on complex policies, procedures and regulatory requirements, preferably in the context of health education environments. Highly developed oral and written communication, stakeholder engagement and relationship management skills, with demonstrated ability to influence and collaborate effectively with stakeholders at all levels. Demonstrated project management and continuous improvement experience, including the ability to lead initiatives, manage competing priorities and deliver outcomes in a complex environment. Demonstrated experience implementing and improving systems, processes and reporting frameworks to enhance operational effectiveness and service delivery. Highly developed digital literacy, including proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and the ability to learn, implement and optimize enterprise systems. Benefits and Culture People are at the core of everything we do. We recognise it is the contributions of our staff who make UNSW one of the best universities in Australia and the world.  Our benefits include: Flexible Working Options (work from home, flexible hours etc) Career development opportunities 17% Superannuation contributions and additional leave loading payments Additional 3 days of leave over Christmas period Discounts and entitlements (retail, education, fitness) How to Apply Make each day matter with a meaningful career at UNSW. Submit your application online before Monday 14th September 2026 at 11:55pm .  Please upload your CV and a document outlining how your skills and experience match the skills and experience listed in the position description (Selection Criteria). A copy of the Position Description can be found on JOBS@UNSW. You should systematically address the selection criteria listed within the position description in your application. Pre-Employment Checks As part of our recruitment process candidates may be required to undergo pre-employment screening, which may include reference checks, qualification verification, right-to-work verification, and criminal history screening where relevant to the role. Get in Touch Anabel Wason Talent Acquisition Partner a.wason@unsw.edu.au Please apply through the application portal and not via the contact above. UNSW is committed to equity diversity and inclusion. Applications from women, people of culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, those living with disabilities, members of the LGBTIQ+ community; and people of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander descent, are encouraged. UNSW provides workplace adjustments for people with disability, and access to flexible work options for eligible staff. The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. Position Description Advertised: 03 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 14 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://external-careers.jobs.unsw.edu.au/en/job/542779/cyber-security-advisor": {
      "title": "Cyber Security Advisor",
      "description": "Cyber Security Advisor Apply now Job no: 542779 Work type: Full Time Location: Sydney, NSW Categories: Information Technology Employment Type: Full Time, 12-month Fixed Term Contract Remuneration: Level 9: From $153,933 + 17% superannuation and leave loading Location: Kensington with transition to newly renovated office at our Randwick campus, anticipated for October 2026 About UNSW At UNSW, we pride ourselves on being a workplace where the best people come to do their best work.  We aspire to be Australia’s global university, improving and transforming lives through excellence in research, outstanding education and a commitment to advancing a just society. About the Role The Business Optimisation Strategy (BOS) is a landmark investment to modernise UNSW’s enterprise platforms and transform service delivery across HR, Finance and IT through the implementation of the ServiceNow and Oracle SaaS platforms. By simplifying processes, improving data foundations, and enabling intelligent automation, BOS supports UNSW’s Progress for All strategy — returning valuable time to staff for teaching, research, and student impact. As BOS mobilises, we are seeking an experienced Cyber Security Advisor to support the operational delivery of an adaptive Cyber Security Governance framework and Information Security Management System (ISMS). This role will play a pivotal part in delivering specialized risk assessments, security assurance, and strategic advisory services to the program and key university stakeholders. By embedding robust information security practices and ongoing operations, the advisor ensures institutional digital assets remain resilient and aligned with governance standards. This role reports directly to the BOS Program Manager – Technology, this individual acts as a primary subject matter expert across the organization. The position carries no direct reports and focuses on evaluating and mitigating risks tied to ICT services and digital initiatives. Responsibilities Deliver expert cyber advisory and risk assessment services to university stakeholders while building strong collaborative relationships. Review system architectures and solution designs to identify risks and produce detailed reporting with actionable treatments. Conduct third-party and supply chain security risk assessments across cloud, AI, identity, ERP, and web technologies. Maintain the cyber risk register by logging, socialising, and tracking risks from projects, pen tests, exemptions, and system changes. Scope and review penetration testing activities, ensuring identified vulnerabilities are assessed, escalated, and remediated. Ensure compliance with security policies, standards, and legal or regulatory requirements, while supporting independent statutory audits. Guide stakeholders on practical security principles, advise on complex exemption requests, and recommend updates to university security policies. About You At least 5 years of experience delivering cyber security risk assessment and advisory services, preferably within global consultancies, tech firms, defence, or large government environments. Relevant tertiary degree paired with extensive experience in cyber security GRC or operations, or an equivalent combination of education and background. Solid GRC fundamentals and deep familiarity with major standards and frameworks such as ISO 27001, ISO 42001, NIST 800-53, Essential 8, and MITRE ATT&CK. Industry certifications such as CISSP (ideal), CISM, CRISC, CEH, or cloud security specialisations (AWS/Azure highly desirable). Strong technical grasp of contemporary security technologies, cloud-native controls, and risk management strategies across complex systems. Exceptional communication, negotiation, and analytical skills to influence stakeholders and translate complex technical concepts for diverse audiences. For further information on the role & responsibilities, please refer to the Position Description. How to Apply: Submit your CV & cover letter detailing your interest and suitability for the job (as per the skills & experience bullet points in the job description ) before 11:55pm Tuesday 15 September 2026. Please note: Sponsorship is not available for this role, valid Australian working rights are required on application. UNSW Benefits and Culture: People are at the core of everything we do. We recognise it is the contributions of our staff who make UNSW one of the best universities in Australia and the world. Our benefits include: Additional 3 days leave during December festive period. Career development opportunities Up to 50% discount on UNSW courses Flexible 17% Superannuation contributions, additional leave-loading payments and salary sacrifice. Discounts and entitlements (retail, education, fitness passport) Job queries contact: Tai James, Talent Acquisition Consultant E: tai.james@unsw.edu.au (applications to the address cannot be accepted, please apply online) UNSW is committed to equity diversity and inclusion. Applications from women, people of culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, those living with disabilities, members of the LGBTIQ+ community; and people of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander descent, are encouraged. UNSW provides workplace adjustments for people with disability, and access to flexible work options for eligible staff. Pre-Employment Checks Aligned with UNSW’s focus on cultivating a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. These pre-employment checks may include a combination of some of the following checks:- National and International Criminal history checks Entitlement to work and ID checks Working With Children Checks Completion of a Gender-Based Violence Prevention Declaration Verification of relevant qualifications Verification of relevant professional membership Employment history and reference checks Financial responsibility assessments/checks. Medical Checks and Assessments Compliance with the necessary combination of these checks is a condition of employment at UNSW. Position Description Advertised: 03 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 15 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://external-careers.jobs.unsw.edu.au/en/job/542909/director-enterprise-data-architecture": {
      "title": "Director, Enterprise Data Architecture",
      "description": "Director, Enterprise Data Architecture Apply now Job no: 542909 Work type: Full Time Location: Sydney, NSW Categories: Information Technology, Professional Leadership Employment Type: Full-time, 12-month Fixed Term role. Remuneration: Competitive total package Location: Kensington, NSW (Hybrid working model) About UNSW At UNSW, we pride ourselves on being a workplace where the best people come to do their best work.  We aspire to be Australia’s global university, improving and transforming lives through excellence in research, outstanding education and a commitment to advancing a just society. Why your role matters This position leads and evolves UNSW’s enterprise data architecture to support University strategy and daily information needs. Reporting to the Chief Data Officer, the role directs the Enterprise Data Architecture capability while establishing governance and driving adoption across all university domains and data custodians. Working closely with leaders across the Enterprise Data Office, UNSW IT, and business units, the position ensures alignment with the Enterprise Data Strategy and incorporates data architecture practices into relevant technology and transformation initiatives. Additionally, the role leverages recognized industry frameworks, monitors emerging sector developments and products, and maintains strong relationships with leading industry suppliers and partners. About the Role The successful applicant will be required to undertake and have experience in the following areas of expertise: Develop and maintain UNSW’s enterprise data architecture to align with strategic priorities, operational needs, and long-term goals. Lead the Enterprise Data Architecture function and roadmap, establishing robust architecture governance, review processes, and fit-for-purpose artifacts. Drive university-wide adoption of enterprise data architecture through targeted initiatives, policies, standards, and domain frameworks. Embed data architecture practices across UNSW IT and university domains, ensuring alignment between strategic planning, solution designs, and project delivery. Oversee data architecture planning and investment advice to deliver sustainable, high-value data capabilities and balance operational risks. Promote higher education data innovation by leveraging industry developments, sector trends, and strategic vendor relationships. Champion data management, governance, privacy, and security practices across the Enterprise Data Office, UNSW IT, and the broader university community. Build, mentor, and lead a high-performing, outcome-driven team while contributing strategically to the broader Enterprise Data Office leadership team. About You Tertiary qualifications in a relevant discipline or equivalent industry experience, backed by extensive leadership expertise in complex environments. Deep technical expertise in enterprise-level data environments, with comprehensive experience across business, application, technology, and integration architecture layers. Proven track record of building respected information architecture capabilities and driving data and technology transformations that deliver strategic business outcomes. Demonstrated experience in strategic planning, operational management, analytical problem-solving, and managing budgets within fast-evolving technology landscapes. Exceptional leadership and talent management skills, with a history of developing, retaining, and guiding high-performing, outcome-focused teams. Outstanding interpersonal, communication, and negotiation abilities, with a strong ability to build trust and influence senior leaders, partners, and vendors. Innovation-driven mindset with a focus on continuous improvement, customer service excellence, ethical standards, and alignment with UNSW values and objectives. For further information on the role & responsibilities, please refer to the Position Description How to Apply: Submit your CV & cover letter detailing your interest and suitability for the job (as per the skills & experience bullet points in the Position Description ) before Sunday 13 th September by 11:55pm. Please note: Sponsorship is not available for this role, valid Australian working rights are required on application. UNSW Benefits and Culture: People are at the core of everything we do. We recognise it is the contributions of our staff who make UNSW one of the best universities in Australia and the world. Our benefits include: Flexible Working Options (work from home, flexible hours etc) Additional 3 days leave during December festive period. Career development opportunities Up to 50% discount on UNSW courses Flexible 17% Superannuation contributions, additional leave-loading payments and salary sacrifice. Discounts and entitlements (retail, education, fitness passport ) UNSW is committed to equity diversity and inclusion. Applications from women, people of culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, those living with disabilities, members of the LGBTIQ+ community; and people of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander descent, are encouraged. UNSW provides workplace adjustments for people with disability, and access to flexible work options for eligible staff. Pre-Employment Checks Aligned with UNSW’s focus on cultivating a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. These pre-employment checks may include a combination of some of the following checks:- National and International Criminal history checks Entitlement to work and ID checks Working With Children Checks Completion of a Gender-Based Violence Prevention Declaration Verification of relevant qualifications Verification of relevant professional membership Employment history and reference checks Financial responsibility assessments/checks. Medical Checks and Assessments Compliance with the necessary combination of these checks is a condition of employment at UNSW. Position Description Advertised: 03 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 13 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://external-careers.jobs.unsw.edu.au/en/job/541532/team-lead-sas": {
      "title": "Team Lead SAS",
      "description": "Team Lead SAS Apply now Job no: 541532 Work type: Full Time Location: Canberra, ACT Categories: Student Services, Management Team Leads – Student Admin Services, UNSW Canberra Employment type: Full-time (35 hours per week) Duration: 1 x continuing/1 x fixed-term contract to 23 December 2027 Remuneration: Level 7 from $118,483 + leave loading + 17% super Location : UNSW Canberra, ADFA Campus Work rights required: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Candidates must hold full rights to work in Australia to be considered for this position. About UNSW Canberra University of New South Wales (UNSW) in Canberra has multiple locations in the Nation’s Capital. UNSW Canberra distinguishes itself from other institutions by its commitment to being thoughtful, practical, and purposeful in all endeavours. This combined approach is integral to the university's impact and contributes to its recognition as one of the top 20 universities globally, as well as a proud member of Australia's esteemed Group of Eight. Choosing a career at UNSW means embracing an environment where thriving, facing challenges, and engaging in meaningful work are not just encouraged but integral to the university experience. If you seek a career where you can excel and contribute meaningfully, you've found the right place. At UNSW, we pride ourselves on being a workplace where the best people come to do their best work. Why Your Role Matters: UNSW Canberra is seeking two experienced and motivated Team Leads – Student Administrative Services to lead a team responsible for delivering high-quality student lifecycle services. These roles are ideal for someone with strong leadership skills, a passion for service excellence, and the ability to drive innovative process improvements across a complex administrative environment. Our ideal candidate is also comfortable with a significant amount of operational oversight, detailed administration, compliance, processing, quality assurance, and workload management. Accountabilities: • Lead and manage a team to deliver high-quality, student-focused administrative services. • Oversee student lifecycle functions including but not limited to admission, orientation, enrolment, assessment and graduation. • Support the development and implementation of student administration procedures and projects with a innovative business improvement focus. • Provide high-level advice and support to students and staff across UNSW Canberra. • Maintain strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders, including Defence partners. • Ensure compliance with university policies, governance, and health and safety standards. Who You Are (skills and experience): • Relevant tertiary qualification and/or extensive experience in student administration and team leadership. • Proven ability to lead, motivate, and develop staff in a dynamic and client-focused environment. • Strong experience across the student lifecycle, including admissions, enrolment, progression, and graduation. • Excellent communication, negotiation, and interpersonal skills. • Demonstrated ability to manage competing priorities and deliver outcomes under pressure. • Experience using complex student systems and data reporting tools. • Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with experience drafting reports, proposals, and business cases. Benefits and Culture: UNSW is committed to helping staff balance work-life responsibilities, by providing access to high-quality services, facilities, and flexible work and leave arrangements. Additional three days leave during December festive period Career development opportunities Up to 50% discount on UNSW courses Flexible 17% superannuation contributions, additional leave-loading payments and salary sacrifice Free gym access UNSW-wide strategy to focus on Healthy Body, Healthy Mind, Healthy Places and Healthy Culture. You can learn more about our Benefits and Culture at Lifestyle & Benefits UNSW Eligibility: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Candidates must hold full rights to work in Australia to be considered for this position. The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. As part of our recruitment process candidates may be required to undergo pre-employment screening, which may include reference checks, qualification verification, right-to-work verification, and criminal history screening where relevant to the role. How to Apply: Make each day matter with a meaningful career at UNSW. Submit your application online before Tuesday 15 September 2026 at 11:30pm , including your CV and a 1–2-page cover letter addressing the required skills and experience outlined in the position description. In order to view the position description, please ensure that you allow pop-ups for https://www.jobs.unsw.edu.au Get in Touch: For role-related queries please contact: Vanessa Dawson - Manager Student Lifecycle v.dawson2@unsw.edu.au For recruitment process-related queries please contact: Holly Whale – Talent Acquisition Partner h.whale@unsw.edu.au Applications cannot be accepted if sent directly to the contact listed. Find out more about the lifestyle and benefits when working with UNSW For further information about UNSW Canberra, please visit: UNSW Canberra For further information on living in Canberra, please visit: Living in Canberra UNSW is committed to equity diversity and inclusion. Applications from women, people of culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, those living with disabilities, members of the LGBTIQ+ community; and people of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander descent, are encouraged. UNSW provides workplace adjustments for people with disability, and access to flexible work options for eligible staff. Position Description Advertised: 02 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 15 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://external-careers.jobs.unsw.edu.au/en/job/542429/program-manager": {
      "title": "Program Manager",
      "description": "Program Manager Apply now Job no: 542429 Work type: Full Time Location: Sydney, NSW Categories: Project Management, Management Employment Type: Full-time, Continuing opportunity. Remuneration: Competitive total package Location: Kensington, NSW (Hybrid working model) About UNSW At UNSW, we pride ourselves on being a workplace where the best people come to do their best work.  We aspire to be Australia’s global university, improving and transforming lives through excellence in research, outstanding education and a commitment to advancing a just society. Why your role matters The Program Manager is a key leadership role within the Enterprise Portfolio Management Office, leading the planning, integration, and delivery of major program initiatives at UNSW. Responsible for setting direction and ensuring operational excellence, the role oversees implementation, change management, data evaluation, and capability development. Leveraging expertise in large-scale operational improvement within complex environments, the position builds and leads a team to execute the program master plan—managing multi-stream schedules, milestones, budgets, interdependencies, and risks. The Program Manager collaborates with leaders across faculties and divisions to provide specialist advice, secure university-wide buy-in, and support project owners and staff. Reporting to the Program Director, the role manages direct reports across several workstreams. About the Role You will be required to undertake and have experience in the following areas of expertise: Provide strategic leadership, advice, and oversight across all program workstreams to meet operational goals and align with UNSW’s mission and compliance requirements. Develop and maintain the program master plan, overseeing multi-stream schedules, key milestones, interdependencies, risks, budgets, and change management. Support project owners through all governance stages, including the preparation of business cases, viability papers, stage gates, and funding requests. Oversee financial management, resource allocation, and continuous improvement initiatives to ensure value, efficient process workflows, and benefit realization. Establish robust risk management practices by proactively identifying, controlling, mitigating, and escalating potential program risks and issues. Direct team operations by coaching, mentoring, and managing performance to foster an inclusive, high-performance execution culture under EPMO frameworks. Lead stakeholder collaboration, change engagement, and transparent communications to secure university-wide buy-in and maintain a strong customer-centric approach. Skills and Experience Relevant tertiary qualifications, industry experience, or an equivalent combination of education, training, and professional practice. Extensive expertise in global transnational education (TNE), with a proven track record of managing end-to-end international programs or work to establish and scale overseas campus operations. Substantial expertise as a Business Analyst, spanning operating models, IT, and comprehensive project management competencies and methodologies. Proven experience in program governance, workload modelling, resource planning, and financial management, including budget oversight and expenditure control. Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with a track record of delivering concise, persuasive executive committee papers, reports, and proposals. Strong leadership capability to manage, coach, and motivate teams while rapidly establishing high credibility and fostering collaborative relationships across stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to drive continuous improvement, resolve complex problems, mitigate risks, and adapt flexibly to changing strategic priorities. For further information on the role & responsibilities, please refer to the Position Description How to Apply: Submit your CV & cover letter detailing your interest and suitability for the job (as per the skills & experience bullet points in the job description ) before Wednesday 16 September by 11:55pm. Please note: Sponsorship is not available for this role, valid Australian working rights are required on application. UNSW Benefits and Culture: People are at the core of everything we do. We recognise it is the contributions of our staff who make UNSW one of the best universities in Australia and the world. Our benefits include: Flexible Working Options (work from home, flexible hours etc) Additional 3 days leave during December festive period. Career development opportunities Up to 50% discount on UNSW courses Flexible 17% Superannuation contributions, additional leave-loading payments and salary sacrifice. Discounts and entitlements (retail, education, fitness passport) Job queries contact: Tai James, Talent Acquisition Consultant E: tai.james@unsw.edu.au (applications to the address cannot be accepted, please apply online) UNSW is committed to equity diversity and inclusion. Applications from women, people of culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, those living with disabilities, members of the LGBTIQ+ community; and people of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander descent, are encouraged. UNSW provides workplace adjustments for people with disability, and access to flexible work options for eligible staff. Pre-Employment Checks Aligned with UNSW’s focus on cultivating a workplace defined by safety, ethical conduct, and strong integrity preferred candidates will be required to participate in a combination of pre-employment checks relevant to the role they have applied for. These pre-employment checks may include a combination of some of the following checks:- National and International Criminal history checks Entitlement to work and ID checks Working With Children Checks Completion of a Gender-Based Violence Prevention Declaration Verification of relevant qualifications Verification of relevant professional membership Employment history and reference checks Financial responsibility assessments/checks. Medical Checks and Assessments Compliance with the necessary combination of these checks is a condition of employment at UNSW. Position Description Advertised: 02 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 16 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
